{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01NS6ExZMygXtrABpmY977fo", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://download.greenpower.org.hk/butterfly/press/20131006_Danaids_e.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://goldcoast.com.hk/en/discover/siu-lang-shui-butterfly-habitat\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/201605/25/P201605250480_print.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://amp.scmp.com/yp/discover/lifestyle/features/article/3063165/butterflies-trail\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/201005/19/P201005190146_print.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.afcd.gov.hk/tc_chi/publications/publications_con/files/hkbonewsletter4.pdf\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nsip-documents.planninginspectorate.gov.uk/published-documents/TR050008-000538-Document\"}, {\"url\": \"https://nsip-documents.planninginspectorate.gov.uk/published-documents/TR050008-000439-Document\"}, {\"url\": \"https://download.greenpower.org.hk/butterfly/press/20180715_Survey_e.pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-20T12:51:15.808Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "\"Siu Lang Shui\" landfill SSSI butterfly designated", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01CvSg7TTi5Cmbef7TJ8muN1", "content": [{"title": "20131006 Danaids e", "url": "https://download.greenpower.org.hk/butterfly/press/20131006_Danaids_e.pdf"}, {"title": "siu lang shui butterfly habitat", "url": "https://goldcoast.com.hk/en/discover/siu-lang-shui-butterfly-habitat"}, {"title": "LCQ3: Setting aside a site at Siu Lang Shui in Tuen Mun for storing idling roadside cargo compartments", "url": "https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/201605/25/P201605250480_print.htm"}, {"title": "butterflies trail", "url": "https://amp.scmp.com/yp/discover/lifestyle/features/article/3063165/butterflies-trail"}, {"title": "LCQ 18: Butterfly assemblages in the hillside of Lung Kwu Tan Village", "url": "https://www.info.gov.hk/gia/general/201005/19/P201005190146_print.htm"}, {"title": "www.afcd.gov.hk", "url": "https://www.afcd.gov.hk/tc_chi/publications/publications_con/files/hkbonewsletter4.pdf"}, {"title": "TR050008 000538 Document 6.6G   ES Appendix 6.7 Butterfly Survey Report Rev A", "url": "https://nsip-documents.planninginspectorate.gov.uk/published-documents/TR050008-000538-Document 6.6G - ES Appendix 6.7 Butterfly Survey Report Rev A.pdf"}, {"title": "TR050008 000439 Document 6.6G   ES Appendix 6.7 Butterfly Survey Report", "url": "https://nsip-documents.planninginspectorate.gov.uk/published-documents/TR050008-000439-Document 6.6G - ES Appendix 6.7 Butterfly Survey Report.pdf"}, {"title": "20180715 Survey e", "url": "https://download.greenpower.org.hk/butterfly/press/20180715_Survey_e.pdf"}]}, "The search didn't turn up a designation date for the Siu Lang Shui SSSI, but it did confirm its status and history.\n\n- **Landfill origin:** The site was a landfill in the 1970s, then closed and was restored in the 1990s.\n- **Butterfly significance:** Green Power describes it as the only Site of Special Scientific Interest (SSSI) in Hong Kong designated for the protection of over-wintering Danaids. It has a peak record of 40,000 overwintering butterflies, per the same source.\n- **Overwintering records:** The first sighting of Danainae overwintering in Siu Lang Shui SSSI was recorded in 1999.\n- **Government reference:** A 2010 Legislative Council reply says Siu Lang Shui and Fung Yuen Valley are listed as Sites of Special Scientific Interest (SSSI), and AFCD has been conducting habitat management on these sites. It gives no designation year.\n\nThe results don't state when Siu Lang Shui was formally designated as an SSSI. For that, check the AFCD SSSI register or the Hong Kong Gazette."], "durationSeconds": 8.080112875000003, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01NS6ExZMygXtrABpmY977fo", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
